  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_010) has been completed, yielding 47.1% accuracy at a high cost of 9.06 GPU hours. This configuration uses transformer aggregation for multiprofile multimodal fusion, which is the most computationally expensive component. Uncertainty: It is unclear whether the transformer aggregation is actually contributing meaningful performance gain over a simpler avgpool, or whether the 47% accuracy is a property of the task/encoders regardless of aggregation. This experiment (config_005) directly ablates the transformer for avgpool while keeping all other settings identical (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, concat fusion), isolating the effect of the aggregation strategy. If avgpool performs comparably, we save substantial GPU hours on all future multiprofile experiments; if transformer is clearly superior, we confirm the investment is warranted. This is the best use of experiment 2 because it reduces the most uncertainty about the single largest cost driver with minimal confounding, and the expected relative cost is moderate (~5-6 GPU hours, roughly 60-65% of config_010's cost) since avgpool is far cheaper than a full transformer over multiple profiles."
}

